            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "D R"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used vegetarian chicken consume powder and replaced 1/3 of the water with milk, but still used the same amount of powder for the amount of liquid.\n\nI also added 1 medium onion, finely diced, and sweated in the butter to make a roux with the flour.\n\nThe milk, I think, makes it smoother when you melt the cheese in. The onion helps round out the flavor.\n\nPS- when adding the grated cheese, leave the stove on LOW and slowly add the cheese, stirring every once in a while. That will keep the cheese from clumping, not melting, and separating."
          },
